      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's introduce the new variable $u=x^{3} - 5.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3 x^{2}\\,⟹\\,1\\text{d}u=3 x^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3 x^{2}\\,{3}^{x^{3} - 5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {3}^{x^{3} - 5}\\cdot 3 x^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\int {3}^{u}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =1\\cdot\\frac{{3}^{u}}{\\ln 3}+C \\\\ & =\\frac{3^{x^{3} - 5}}{\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
